<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What a Joomla site reads when its administrator presses "Check For Updates".

    Reached because `pkg_claudecowork.xml` declares this address as the extension's update server.
    Joomla records that address when the package is INSTALLED, so only sites running 0.8.1 or
    later ever ask for this file — an older copy has no update site and must be updated once by
    hand (or by Tracy Desk) before it can update itself.

    One entry per released version, newest first. Joomla picks the highest version whose
    targetplatform matches the site it runs on, so leaving old entries in place costs nothing and
    lets a site on an older Joomla still find the last version that supported it.

    Bump it in the same commit that bumps the manifest: tests/run.php fails if the two disagree.
-->
